# LF in the repository and LF on checkout, on every platform. This is a cross-platform library,
# and pinning the ending here rather than relying on each clone's core.autocrlf is what keeps
# `dotnet format --verify-no-changes` passing identically on Linux, macOS and Windows. It matches
# end_of_line = lf in .editorconfig; the two must agree or the format gate fails.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Batch files are the genuine exception: cmd.exe requires CRLF, and a LF-only .cmd can fail in
# ways that are hard to read. PowerShell is happy with LF, so .ps1 is left alone.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary files: never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.snk binary
*.gz  binary

# Generated emoji packs are Brotli-compressed and must stay byte-exact, or regeneration would
# appear to change data it did not touch.
*.br binary
